From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SplitPlay <splitplay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 21:13:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] splitplay: capture on frame arrival (capture_mode),
 capture_fps

Upstream's DDA loop sleeps to the stream's next frame slot
(group start + k/fps) and only then takes the newest desktop frame, so a
frame DWM composes just after a slot waits up to one stream interval:
half an interval on average, about 8 ms at 60 fps, unless the game
happens to be locked to the slots.

New profile field capture_mode (docs/contracts/ipc.md), live:

- slot (default, upstream's loop unchanged);
- arrival: wait in AcquireNextFrame and hand each frame to the encoder
  as soon as it comes. Desktop Duplication accumulates what DWM composes
  while the loop waits, so the frame taken is always the newest. A rate
  budget keeps the average at the stream's frame rate: frames are at
  least 3/4 of an interval apart, each spends one interval of budget,
  and at most one interval can be saved up while frames are sparse.
  The minimum frame rate is still kept up by the encoder (min_fps).

A change of mode is logged and restarts the pacing state; the profile
setter is one atomic read per frame.

The heartbeat's metrics gain capture_fps: the frames DWM composed per
second, summed from DXGI_OUTDUPL_FRAME_INFO::AccumulatedFrames of every
acquired frame with a present time (pointer-only updates are skipped).
It is the session's real composition rate whatever the capture mode,
not the rate the loop samples at, and null while no stream runs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J21Rm4ZuX6wPwWNnDdGg8u

